{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5c3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c836-a2d8-7092-9401-37d2858a2ec3"},"sequence":316,"recorded_at":1780531400000627,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a68a1bdc-1b82-44d2-b715-51014e29fd57","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"a68a1bdc-1b82-44d2-b715-51014e29fd57","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a68a1bdc-1b82-44d2-b715-51014e29fd57"},"call_id":"call_01a0c8376d6172059b2b96f68d89c2e9","text":"Read text file `/tmp/1c28dz/TASK-260830-1c28dz_results.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-1c28dz — Producer results, rev4 (tmux lifecycle operations)\n2|\n3|Revision-4 rework on checkpoint `d4bd91d0` (STORY-260830-2t4g7i\n4|worktree, branch `task-board/story/STORY-260830-2t4g7i`,\n5|uncommitted). Closes the three rev3 P1s, P2-A, P2-B, and the four\n6|surviving narrowings plus the SPW custody fifth. Production `.go`\n7|delta is purely additive (0 deleted lines across the three touched\n8|landed files; every other production file is new) — see\n9|`grid/additive_diff.txt`.\n10|\n11|## Revision-4 fixes (reviewer P1/P2/R1-R5)\n12|\n13|P1-A (quiescence fails open after state write fails;\n14|`internal/tmuxserver/lifecycle.go:executeEngineOp`,\n15|`ops.go:checkAttachQuiesced`, `state.go:QuiesceBarrierProven`).\n16|The barrier write is fail-closed now: quiesce-input and\n17|wait-safe-boundary return `terminal_backend_integrity_failure`\n18|at `quiesce/boundary state image` when their memory write fails,\n19|and the closure-outcome report commits BEFORE the memory write\n20|so the identical retry replays the original closure time and\n21|heals the barrier. When the memory holds no record, attach\n22|recovers the barrier from the completed quiesce/boundary\n23|outcomes for the instance instead of mistaking the loss for an\n24|open input; a corrupt scan or an empty closure time errors.\n25|Non-barrier operations keep advisory memory (their lost writes\n26|never admit input — pinned by\n27|`TestRecordFailureLeavesPresenceReconciliation`). Five committed\n28|tests\n29|(`TestExecuteQuiesceStateWriteFailureRefusesWiredAttach`,\n30|`TestExecuteQuiesceRetryAfterStateWriteFailureHealsBarrier`,\n31|`TestExecuteBoundaryBarrierSurvivesStateWriteFailure`,\n32|`TestExecuteAttachErrorsOnCorruptBarrierScan`,\n33|`TestExecuteAttachErrorsOnEmptyBarrierTime/quiesce,boundary`)\n34|drive the reviewer 2-call sequence plus healing, boundary-arm\n35|isolation, corrupt-scan, and empty-time shapes through\n36|`Execute` with literal code assertions. Seven narrowing rows\n37|(`N-quiesce-state-record`, `N-boundary-state-record`,\n38|`N-attach-barrier-quiesce-recovery`,\n39|`N-attach-barrier-boundary-recovery`,\n40|`N-attach-barrier-corrupt-scan`,\n41|`N-attach-barrier-empty-quiesce`,\n42|`N-attach-barrier-empty-boundary`) KILLED; the pre-existing\n43|`N-quiesce-attach-gate` row re-anchored to the restructured\n44|check and still KILLED.\n45|\n46|P1-B (refreshed lease decision not bound to executed restore;\n47|`internal/tmuxserver/wrapper.go:checkRestoreWinnerBound`). The\n48|launch/reattach arms refuse `local_precondition_failed` at\n49|`wrapper restore winner binding` before any effect unless the\n50|carried restore authorization `(lease_id, lease_epoch)` equals\n51|the ordered winner — the decision, the binding, and the backend\n52|restore (which still authorizes against the current lease)\n53|form one authorization. Backend restore authorization is\n54|never weakened to make the join fit. Three committed tests\n55|(`TestWrapperRestoreRefusesDivergentWinner` — the reviewer\n56|sequence — plus `...Lease` and `...Epoch` single-arm\n57|isolations) and two narrowing rows\n58|(`N-wrapper-winner-lease`, `N-wrapper-winner-epoch`) KILLED.\n59|The honest launch/reattach tests (winner == carried auth)\n60|still execute.\n61|\n62|P1-C (expired refresh accepted; bound only cooperative;\n63|`internal/tmuxserver/wrapper.go:refreshWinner`). The adapter\n64|runs on its own goroutine and the entry takes whichever\n65|answers first — the adapter or the deadline. Late answers\n66|never verify even with a nil error (expiry is checked on the\n67|answer path too, because both arms can be ready at once), and\n68|a non-cooperative adapter loses at the bound (measured 9.9ms\n69|wall for a 1ms bound against a 100ms ignoring adapter).\n70|`TestWrapperRestoreRefreshRaceRejectsLateAnswer` stalls the\n71|select hook twenty times past the bound to force the\n72|both-ready race deterministically (20/20 parks; the expired\n73|mutant kills through it twice-verified). The cooperative\n74|`configured-50ms` subtest dropped its shared-var observation\n75|(unsynchronized by design under enforcement — it would race)\n76|and tightened elapsed 5s→1s. Two narrowing rows\n77|(`N-wrapper-refresh-expired`, `N-wrapper-refresh-deadline`)\n78|KILLED. Bound B37 states the missing production mesh\n79|transport: the composition enforces the bound on any injected\n80|adapter.\n81|\n82|R1-R5 (reviewer narrowings; corrected R5 plant). Five committed\n83|clause witnesses through the production entries\n84|(`TestExecuteStatusAttachedExitIsUnknown`,\n85|`TestExecuteStatusForeignAttachedRowIsUnknown`,\n86|`TestExecuteStatusUnknownPanesExitIsUnknown`,\n87|`TestOSRunnerRefusesNulArgument`,\n88|`TestServerSpawnerRefusesWritableRoot`) plus five harness rows\n89|with the reviewer's exact plants\n90|(`N-status-attached-exit`, `N-status-foreign-row`,\n91|`N-status-panes-unknown-exit`, `N-osrunner-argv-nul`,\n92|`N-spawn-root-custody`) KILLED. The SPW rootwrite cell moves\n93|B39→M, closing the already-owned spawner custody bound.\n94|\n95|P2-B (census/prose). Table C 19→18 U2c (18 names listed);\n96|totals recomputed by script over the tables (238 measured of\n97|4896; 181 bound; 4477 unreachable); resume-reachable status\n98|cells reclassified U2a/U1→B39 (20 cells across 10 rows:\n99|statusunbound, statusdoc, statusmatch, statusnegative,\n100|absentmemory, presentmemory, attachable, cutrow, emptypanes,\n101|triple); row 83 drops the five removed test names and\n102|corrects the order claim (prior validation precedes effects;\n103|the successor persists after); intro 92/92; wall-time prose\n104|corrected (three wrapper refresh tests measure elapsed time);\n105|Table E grows 13→17 outcomes; symmetry paragraph covers the\n106|revision-4 sidedness (rootwrite gains SPW 1).\n107|\n108|P2-A (outcome grid over the importer closure; `grid/`). Entry\n109|grid: drivers `zz_grid_p_test.go` (pre-existing entries, both\n110|trees) and `zz_grid_n_test.go` (new entries, candidate only)\n111|emit `{package, entry, input, outcome, code, digest}` JSONL.\n112|Pre-existing tmuxserver (18 keys) + termbind (9 keys): zero\n113|moves. New entries (25 + 2 keys): all ADDED, none on the base.\n114|Suite grid: `go test -json ./...` on the base worktree and the\n115|candidate, diffed keyed `(package, test) → pass|fail|skip`\n116|over the 34-package production closure: 23,054 shared keys,\n117|zero moves, 476 additions (471 tmuxserver + 5 termbind, all\n118|pass), zero removed. Blast radius is `{tmuxserver,\n119|termbind}` — nothing imports either except tmuxserver→termbind\n120|— and no production `.go` line outside them changed.\n121|Exclusions stated: crashgate/environ (test-only deps,\n122|pass→pass, included in the streams); store-backed termbind\n123|entries excluded from the entry grid (covered by the suites);\n124|timing-sensitive tests are the three candidate-only\n125|wall-clock wrapper tests. Drivers, raw streams, diff reports,\n126|and the additive diff ship in the tarball.\n127|\n128|## Mutant battery\n129|\n130|tmuxserver (`harness_chunk1.log`..`harness_chunk4.log`,\n131|`harness/`):\n132|\n133|- 251/251 rows as expected: 250 KILLED (248 narrowing `N-*`\n134|  + 2 additive `D-*`) and `C-control` SURVIVED (harmless\n135|  comment-only control, shared with the first leaf).\n136|- One raw log per plant under `harness/` (251 files).\n137|- All four chunks ran after the final code/test/harness\n138|  edits in this session (exit 0 each). The only post-harness\n139|  delta is prose (`TRACEABILITY.md`, matrix, `README.md`,\n140|  `LOGBOOK.md`, results), which no harness row reads; the\n141|  package suite re-ran green after every edit.\n142|\n143|termbind (`harness_termbind.log`):\n144|\n145|- 40/40 rows as expected: 38 narrowing `N-*` + 1\n146|  supplementary `D-*` KILLED, `C-control` SURVIVED, including\n147|  the 4 reboot-successor rows. Re-ran after the final edits\n148|  (exit 0).\n149|\n150|Combined: 291/291 rows as expected, zero mismatches.\n151|\n152|## Acceptance criteria\n153|\n154|34 of 34 tmuxserver rows (TRACEABILITY rows 59-92) driven\n155|through production entries by named tests, plus termbind row\n156|67 (successor mint); see\n157|`TASK-260830-1c28dz_conformance-matrix.md` (AC table +\n158|per-section mirrors + dispatch-arm table + gate x entry\n159|census Tables B/C/D + Table E + bounds + battery; clause,\n160|census, and bounds mirrors verified byte-identical to the\n161|package TRACEABILITY by script). Eight of eight lifecycle\n162|operations driven through `Execute` (ops table in the\n163|matrix), plus the after-restore composition entry.\n164|\n165|## OUTCOME-keyed base-vs-candidate comparison (`grid/`)\n166|\n167|Entry grid (`entry_diff.txt`, drivers under\n168|`grid/tmuxserver/` + `grid/termbind/`, raw `grid_*.jsonl`):\n169|\n170|- Pre-existing tmuxserver entries (Acquire, SocketPath,\n171|  ResolveSocket, BuildArgv, CheckServerAttested,\n172|  CheckBrokerContact, Ensure/VerifyRuntimeDir,\n173|  ObserveAmbient): 18 keys, zero moves.\n174|- Pre-existing termbind entries (ParseTerminalBinding,\n175|  CheckInstanceIdentity, AdmitMutationContext,\n176|  AdmitStatusBody): 9 keys, zero moves.\n177|- New entries (Lifecycle.Execute 8 ops admitted/refused,\n178|  ExecuteWrapperRestore launch/divergent, InstanceStates,\n179|  BuildCommand, CheckSocketLength/Custody,\n180|  MintSuccessorBinding): 27 keys, all ADDED — the base has\n181|  no such entries.\n182|\n183|Suite grid (`suite_diff.txt`, raw `suite_base.json` /\n184|`suite_candidate.json`, base from a detached worktree at\n185|`d4bd91d0`, candidate from this tree), keyed\n186|`(package, test) → pass|fail|skip` over the 34-package\n187|production closure:\n188|\n189|- Base: 23,054 keys. Candidate: 23,530 keys.\n190|- MOVED: 0. ADDED: 476 (all pass; 471 tmuxserver + 5\n191|  termbind). REMOVED: 0. No package outcome moves.\n192|- crashgate/environ: pass→pass (test-only deps, in-stream).\n193|\n194|Inputs that moved across an admission/refusal arm are all\n195|inside the new leaf (no pre-existing entry changed behavior\n196|— 27/27 grid keys plus 23,054/23,054 suite keys retained\n197|prove it): barrier-state failures now fail the operation\n198|instead of reporting closure; divergent wrapper winners\n199|refuse instead of executing; expired/late refreshes park\n200|instead of resuming; exit-1 attached, foreign attached rows,\n201|exit-2 panes, NUL argv, and writable spawn roots refuse at\n202|their entries. Each moved input has a named negative test\n203|and a narrowing row above.\n204|\n205|## Validation gates (all exit 0; logs in the tarball)\n206|\n207|- gofmt clean, `go build ./...`, `go vet ./...` unix and\n208|  windows, `git diff --check`, windows build.\n209|- `go test ./... -count=1` (also as `suite_candidate.json`).\n210|- `go test -race -count=1` on tmuxserver and termbind.\n211|- `go test -cover`: tmuxserver 87.7%, termbind 83.5%.\n212|- tracecheck, cataloggen clean, catalog pin, specdoc suites\n213|  green (inside the full run).\n214|- No-tmux run: `tmux` absent from PATH (`NO_TMUX`\n215|  asserted), both touched packages pass (`v-notmux.log`).\n216|- `task-board validate`: exit 0, 179 pre-existing\n217|  missing-activity notes, none on this task (`v-board.log`).\n218|- Fuzz: no `Fuzz` targets exist in the touched packages\n219|  (grep-verified); fuzz seed corpora of the untouched\n220|  packages run inside the full suite.\n221|\n222|## Real-tmux witnesses\n223|\n224|Zero: no committed test execs a real tmux or dials a real\n225|socket (`v-notmux.log`). Three wrapper refresh tests measure\n226|wall-clock elapsed time against generous bounds (enforcement\n227|is timing by definition); every other test runs on the\n228|manual clock. Every AC row is witnessed deterministically\n229|only.\n230|\n231|## Census (second leaf)\n232|\n233|Table B 24x21 (10 M, 494 U2a), Table C 129x11 (1401 U2a,\n234|18 U2c), Table D 129x21 (178 M, 177 B, 2354 U; counts\n235|verified by script over the table), Table E 17 after-restore\n236|outcomes; totals 238 measured of 4896 with 181 bound and\n237|4477 unreachable with reasons. Bounds B1-B39 (B37 filled):\n238|27 driven-but-rowless cells and 150 named undriven gaps (142\n239|of them the B39 reachable-undriven reclass), each with its\n240|owner in the matrix.\n241|\n242|## Handoff\n243|\n244|Ready for review. Worktree intentionally UNCOMMITTED for\n245|Story handoff snapshot (no commits on the Story branch this\n246|run). Attachments: this file (standalone), the conformance\n247|matrix, and `TASK-260830-1c28dz_rework-evidence-rev4.tar.gz`.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
