{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c725","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c836-a2d8-7092-9401-37d2858a2ec3"},"sequence":493,"recorded_at":1780531400000981,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a68a1bdc-1b82-44d2-b715-51014e29fd57","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"a68a1bdc-1b82-44d2-b715-51014e29fd57","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a68a1bdc-1b82-44d2-b715-51014e29fd57"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c837-c9d1-7ca3-a82e-e3c0aa50d57e"},"task_id":"01a0c837-c9d1-7ca3-a82e-e3c0aa50d57e","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c837-c9d1-7ca3-a82e-e3c0aa50d57e","chunk":"Read text file `internal/tmuxserver/wrapper.go`.\n1|package tmuxserver\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"context\"\n5|\t\"time\"\n6|\n7|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/axpane\"\n8|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/fencing\"\n9|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/sessrepo\"\n10|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/terminalbackend\"\n11|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/terminstance\"\n12|)\n13|\n14|// This file orders the §4.2 after-restore sequence at the wrapper\n15|// composition entry: read the latest locally known lease, attempt the\n16|// mesh lease refresh under the measured bound, then decide through\n17|// the landed wrapper owner and route to the decided effects. The\n18|// backend restore entry stays the narrow §4.C row — recreate the\n19|// wrapper under restore authorization and return the parked wire\n20|// result — while this entry owns the order: the refresh runs before\n21|// the decision, so a lapsed local grant under a refreshed remote\n22|// winner offers remote attach instead of refusing at backend\n23|// authorization that the offer path never reaches. Backend restore\n24|// authorization is never weakened to make that path pass: the offer\n25|// and park branches run no backend operation at all.\n26|\n27|// WrapperRestoreRequest is one after-restore composition: the wrapper\n28|// decision input the caller built (mode restore), the local fencing\n29|// facts the ordered observation carries, and the backend restore\n30|// request the resume branches execute.\n31|type WrapperRestoreRequest struct {\n32|\t// Decide is the complete wrapper decision input. Mode must be\n33|\t// restore; Observation is ordered here (the caller-supplied one\n34|\t// is replaced by the refreshed/local observation), every other\n35|\t// member passes through to the landed owner.\n36|\tDecide axpane.Input\n37|\t// Grant is the process-local fencing authorization with its\n38|\t// policy, observed over the ordered winner. Presence is\n39|\t// required; expiry is the landed direction-first arm's verdict,\n40|\t// so a lapsed grant under a remote winner still parks remote\n41|\t// instead of refusing.\n42|\tGrant    sessrepo.FencingGrant\n43|\tHasGrant bool\n44|\tPolicy   sessrepo.FencingPolicy\n45|\t// Restore is the backend restore request the launch and reattach\n46|\t// branches execute. Operation must be restore; the entry\n47|\t// executes nothing else.\n48|\tRestore OpRequest\n49|}\n50|\n51|// WrapperRestoreOutcome is one composed after-restore result: the\n52|// ordered decision, the refresh audit, the winner the decision ran\n53|// over, and the backend restore outcome on the resume branches only.\n54|type WrapperRestoreOutcome struct {\n55|\t// Decision is the landed wrapper verdict: launch, reattach,\n56|\t// attach_remote, takeover_offer, parked, or refused.\n57|\tDecision axpane.Decision\n58|\t// RefreshAttempted reports that the mesh refresh ran; RefreshSucceeded\n59|\t// reports that it answered (a missing adapter, a failed attempt, and\n60|\t// a timed-out attempt all fall back to local knowledge unverified).\n61|\tRefreshAttempted bool\n62|\tRefreshSucceeded bool\n63|\t// RefreshBoundMs is the measured bound one attempt ran under.\n64|\tRefreshBoundMs uint64\n65|\t// WinnerLeaseID and WinnerHostID name the winning lease the\n66|\t// decision ran over: the refreshed winner, or the locally known\n67|\t// lease when the refresh did not answer.\n68|\tWinnerLeaseID string\n69|\tWinnerHostID  string\n70|\t// Restore is the backend restore outcome on launch and reattach,\n71|\t// nil on every other branch (those branches run no backend\n72|\t// operation and launch no provider).\n73|\tRestore *OpOutcome\n74|}\n75|\n76|// ExecuteWrapperRestore runs the §4.2 after-restore sequence to its\n77|// decided effects:\n78|//\n79|//  1. read the latest locally known lease (CurrentLease);\n80|//  2. attempt the mesh lease refresh under the measured bound (a\n81|//     missing, failed, or timed-out attempt falls back to local\n82|//     knowledge, unverified — never verified, never blocking\n83|//     forever);\n84|//  3. decide through the landed wrapper owner over the ordered\n85|//     winner (local win plus valid materialization resumes);\n86|//  4. offer remote attach/takeover when another host owns the session\n87|//     in an interactive terminal;\n88|//  5. park without launching the provider in all other cases.\n89|//\n90|// Only the launch and reattach decisions execute the backend restore,\n91|// and only bound to the decided winner: the restore authorization\n92|// must carry the ordered (lease_id, lease_epoch), so a refreshed\n93|// winner for one lease never authorizes effects under another\n94|// lease's grant. The offer, park, and refuse decisions return with\n95|// no backend operation, no tmux exec, and no provider. Union-rival\n96|// ambiguity is not modeled here (bound B38): the entry decides over\n97|// the single refreshed or local winner, and a refresh adapter that\n98|// observes rivals must surface them as refresh failure so the entry\n99|// parks unverified.\n100|func (lc *Lifecycle) ExecuteWrapperRestore(ctx context.Context, req WrapperRestoreRequest) (WrapperRestoreOutcome, error) {\n101|\tempty := WrapperRestoreOutcome{}\n102|\tif lc == nil || lc.CurrentLease == nil || lc.CurrentGeneration == nil || lc.Now == nil ||\n103|\t\tlc.Runner == nil || lc.Receipts == nil || lc.Bindings == nil || lc.Attach == nil || lc.States == nil {\n104|\t\treturn empty, &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodeProtocolError, Detail: \"lifecycle dependencies\"}\n105|\t}\n106|\tif req.Decide.Mode != axpane.ModeRestore {\n107|\t\treturn empty, &Error{Code: CodeInvalidArguments, Detail: \"wrapper restore mode\"}\n108|\t}\n109|\tif req.Restore.Operation != string(terminalbackend.OperationRestore) {\n110|\t\treturn empty, &Error{Code: CodeInvalidArguments, Detail: \"wrapper restore operation\"}\n111|\t}\n112|\tlocal := lc.CurrentLease()\n113|\tbound := lc.MeshRefreshTimeout\n114|\tif bound <= 0 {\n115|\t\tbound = DefaultMeshRefreshTimeout\n116|\t}\n117|\twinner, verified, attempted, succeeded := lc.refreshWinner(ctx, req.Decide.SessionID, local, bound)\n118|\tnow := lc.Now()\n119|\tinput := req.Decide\n120|\tinput.Observation = fencing.Observation{\n121|\t\tSessionID:   req.Decide.SessionID,\n122|\t\tWinner:      winner,\n123|\t\tHasWinner:   winner.LeaseID != \"\" && winner.Epoch != 0,\n124|\t\tLocalHostID: lc.LocalHostID,\n125|\t\tVerified:    verified,\n126|\t\tGrant:       req.Grant,\n127|\t\tHasGrant:    req.HasGrant,\n128|\t\tPolicy:      req.Policy,\n129|\t\tNow:         now,\n130|\t}\n131|\tdecision := axpane.Decide(input)\n132|\toutcome := WrapperRestoreOutcome{\n133|\t\tDecision:         decision,\n134|\t\tRefreshAttempted: attempted,\n135|\t\tRefreshSucceeded: succeeded,\n136|\t\tRefreshBoundMs:   uint64(bound.Milliseconds()),\n137|\t\tWinnerLeaseID:    winner.LeaseID,\n138|\t\tWinnerHostID:     winner.HolderHostID,\n139|\t}\n140|\tswitch decision.Action {\n141|\tcase axpane.ActionLaunch, axpane.ActionReattach:\n142|\t\tif err := checkRestoreWinnerBound(req.Restore.Body, winner); err != nil {\n143|\t\t\treturn outcome, err\n144|\t\t}\n145|\t\trestored, err := lc.Execute(ctx, req.Restore)\n146|\t\toutcome.Restore = &restored\n147|\t\tif err != nil {\n148|\t\t\treturn outcome, err\n149|\t\t}\n150|\t\treturn outcome, nil\n151|\tdefault:\n152|\t\treturn outcome, nil\n153|\t}\n154|}\n155|\n156|// checkRestoreWinnerBound binds the executed backend restore to the\n157|// lease the wrapper decision just ran over: the restore\n158|// authorization's (lease_id, lease_epoch) must equal the ordered\n159|// winner. The decision authorizes the winner and the backend\n160|// authorizes the restore against the current lease, but neither ties\n161|// the two together — without this join a refreshed winner for one\n162|// lease would authorize effects under another lease's grant, two\n163|// gates passing over different leases. A malformed restore body\n164|// refuses its own parse error (the same refusal the backend entry\n165|// would return), and a divergent authorization refuses the failed\n166|// local precondition before any effect runs. Backend restore\n167|// authorization is never weakened to make the join fit: this gate\n168|// only refuses what the decision did not select.\n169|func checkRestoreWinnerBound(raw []byte, winner sessrepo.LeaseSummary) error {\n170|\tbody, err := parseRestoreBody(raw)\n171|\tif err != nil {\n172|\t\treturn err\n173|\t}\n174|\tif body.Context.Authorization.LeaseID != winner.LeaseID ||\n175|\t\tbody.Context.Authorization.LeaseEpoch != winner.Epoch {\n176|\t\treturn &Error{Code: terminalbackend.CodePreconditionFailed, Detail: \"wrapper restore winner binding\"}\n177|\t}\n178|\treturn nil\n179|}\n180|\n181|// refreshResult is one mesh lease-refresh answer from the adapter\n182|// goroutine.\n183|type refreshResult struct {\n184|\twinner RefreshWinner\n185|\terr    error\n186|}\n187|\n188|// refreshWinner attempts the §4.2 mesh lease refresh (step 2) under\n189|// the measured bound and reports the ordered winner: the refreshed\n190|// lease verified on success, the locally known lease unverified when\n191|// the adapter is missing, fails, or times out, and the zero winner\n192|// when no lease is known at all. Only a successful refresh verifies:\n193|// local knowledge never self-verifies, so a failed attempt parks\n194|// through the landed unverified arm instead of resuming.\n195|//\n196|// The bound is enforced, never cooperative: the adapter runs on its\n197|// own goroutine and the entry takes whichever answers first — the\n198|// adapter or the deadline. An adapter that ignores cancellation\n199|// still loses at the bound, and an answer that arrives after the\n200|// deadline elapsed is rejected even with a nil error (the expiry is\n201|// checked on the answer path too, because both arms can be ready at\n202|// once). The abandoned adapter send never blocks — the channel is\n203|// buffered — and its goroutine exits when the adapter returns, so\n204|// nothing here waits past the bound.\n205|func (lc *Lifecycle) refreshWinner(ctx context.Context, sessionID string, local terminstance.LeaseView, bound time.Duration) (sessrepo.LeaseSummary, bool, bool, bool) {\n206|\tfallback := sessrepo.LeaseSummary{\n207|\t\tSessionID:    sessionID,\n208|\t\tLeaseID:      local.LeaseID,\n209|\t\tEpoch:        local.Epoch,\n210|\t\tHolderHostID: lc.LocalHostID,\n211|\t\tReason:       \"local-knowledge\",\n212|\t}\n213|\tif lc.LeaseRefresh == nil {\n214|\t\treturn fallback, false, false, false\n215|\t}\n216|\trefreshCtx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(ctx, bound)\n217|\tdefer cancel()\n218|\tanswered := make(chan refreshResult, 1)\n219|\tgo func() {\n220|\t\twinner, err := lc.LeaseRefresh(refreshCtx, sessionID)\n221|\t\tanswered <- refreshResult{winner: winner, err: err}\n222|\t}()\n223|\tif lc.RefreshHooks != nil && lc.RefreshHooks.BeforeSelect != nil {\n224|\t\tlc.RefreshHooks.BeforeSelect()\n225|\t}\n226|\tselect {\n227|\tcase result := <-answered:\n228|\t\tif result.err != nil || refreshCtx.Err() != nil {\n229|\t\t\treturn fallback, false, true, false\n230|\t\t}\n231|\t\treturn sessrepo.LeaseSummary{\n232|\t\t\tSessionID:    sessionID,\n233|\t\t\tLeaseID:      result.winner.LeaseID,\n234|\t\t\tEpoch:        result.winner.Epoch,\n235|\t\t\tHolderHostID: result.winner.HolderHostID,\n236|\t\t\tReason:       \"mesh-refresh\",\n237|\t\t}, true, true, true\n238|\tcase <-refreshCtx.Done():\n239|\t\treturn fallback, false, true, false\n240|\t}\n241|}","final_result":true}}}
