emory assertion fails (admission still refuses via the proof, which is the construction). [exit 1]\\nok: N-create-incarnation-record: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the fixture instance past the fail-closed create rotation; every other instance still fails closed. Kill path: the create reports success after its rotation failed. [exit 1]\\nok: N-restore-incarnation-record: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the fixture instance past the fail-closed restore rotation; every other instance still fails closed. Kill path: the restore reports success after its rotation failed. [exit 1]\\nMISMATCH: N-create-replay-skip: SURVIVED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the fixture instance past the replay-rotation skip (its replay rotates); every other replay still skips. Kill path: the replayed create erases the newer closure and the attach succeeds. [exit 0]\\nMISMATCH: D-restore-replay-rotation: SURVIVED (want KILLED) :: Supplementary additive plant (not a narrowing): the restore replay skip is structural (no code to weaken), so this plant inserts the forbidden rotation to prove the test observes it. Kill path: the replayed restore erases the newer closure and the attach succeeds. [exit 0]\\nok: N-terminate-no-rotation: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly terminate-stale past the restore-only rotation arm; the restore rotation itself is unchanged. Kill path: the terminate rotates and the incarnation-absent assertion fails. [exit 1]\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 2248,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 562,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
