{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000f299","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c836-a2d8-7092-9401-37d2858a2ec3"},"sequence":6055,"recorded_at":1780531400012105,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a68a1bdc-1b82-44d2-b715-51014e29fd57","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"a68a1bdc-1b82-44d2-b715-51014e29fd57","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a68a1bdc-1b82-44d2-b715-51014e29fd57"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c868-1da0-7223-8bd9-f42f767f17d2"},"task_id":"01a0c868-1da0-7223-8bd9-f42f767f17d2","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c868-1da0-7223-8bd9-f42f767f17d2","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-161-1\",\n  \"command\": \"tail -n 30 LOGBOOK.md; echo \\\"===git-diff-loogbook===\\\"; git diff LOGBOOK.md | head -n 20\",\n  \"description\": \"Check logbook tail\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"- BASE: unchanged from rev8: candidate checkpoint `305875134f8d344eb86ef926c7fbca3fed85c49d`, protected AX trunk `8626fb361c1d6b62d5f95c7be4cb33c85d4aadf3`. The 15-file RPC backup manifest, parked RPC delta, and checkpointed SSH/peer work remain preserved; no RPC implementation path was absorbed.\\n- FIX (F1): the production-source write-path census now resolves `go/types` function identities for bare identifiers and selectors, while rejecting writer-shaped indirect callees unless they are an exact censused definition in the current Go build context. The census rejects dot-imported function values, promoted embedded backend methods, package-level slice writer functions, function-typed struct fields and parameters, and dot-imported composite-literal function values. `isHoldEntryCall` uses exact package/receiver/method identity, so a same-named impostor method is not an entry gate.\\n- FIX (F2): `WithExclusiveHoldForConfig` is Store-owned. A generic or foreign Store cannot bind an arbitrary existing Config path; a configured Store can bind only its canonical paired path. Refusal occurs before staging/bytes mutation. The narrowing mutant drops the unconfigured-store refusal while retaining the other path checks and is killed by `TestWithExclusiveHoldForConfigRefusesUnconfiguredStorePath`.\\n- EVIDENCE: `writepath-method-value-skip` preserves the searched token while weakening the typed method-value gate and is killed by `TestWritePathGateFlagsExecutableRogues/backend_method_value`; controls have executable witnesses for all six CR8 shapes. Hosttrust `hold-resource-skip` is killed by the unconfigured foreign-resource test. Final artifacts are under `.temp/TASK-260909-2ez769/mutations-{config,hosttrust}-rev9/`.\\n- COVERAGE RATIO: 19 of 21 enumerated production acceptance rows are driven by named production-entry tests. The two stated bounds remain: Windows runtime DACL execution is not available on this Darwin runner, and this repository has no export/replication consumer surface for host-trust secret exclusion. No claim is made for either bound.\\n- VALIDATION: grouped full suite `go test -count=1 -v` A/B/C/D all exit 0 across all 26 packages; grouped full coverage A/B/C/D all exit 0 (`config 93.5%`, `hosttrust 77.9%`, `peeridentity 97.5%`); scoped hosttrust/config/peeridentity tests, scoped vet, native/Linux-arm64/Windows-amd64 builds, Windows test compilation, `go mod tidy -diff`, and `git diff --check` are green. Logs and package inventory are in `.temp/TASK-260909-2ez769/`.\\n- STATUS: ready for review; worktree remains intentionally UNCOMMITTED for Story handoff snapshot.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-1c28dz rework rev2 — rev1 CHANGES REQUESTED repaired on checkpoint 1ba06e9\\n- SCOPE: second leaf of STORY-260830-2t4g7i, tmux lifecycle operations. All five P1 + two P2 closed in `internal/tmuxserver`; trunk unmoved, no rebase. Only touched landed files: error-code registry (new codes), ownership seam (test hook), mutant harness (new rows).\\n- P1-A: boundary vector is the bare blocking `wait-for <channel>` (no `-L`); proof kind carried engine→evidence with provider rows as best-effort context; quiesce barrier = `lock-session` then `detach-client -s` with AX-side input-attach refusal once quiescing; no `send-keys` from quiesce. Bound B33: wrapper `wait-for -S` signal unimplemented, waits time out fail-closed.\\n- P1-B: `BuildCommand` emits `attach-session -r` iff `input_authorized=false`; unstated authorization refuses at the execution boundary.\\n- P1-C: `RunResult` carries stderr; signal deaths error and prove nothing; `classifyAbsence` proves absence only from exit + stderr marker (tmux 3.6a verified), everything else unknown at all three consumers (probe/poll/terminate). Bound B35: other tmux versions fail closed.\\n- P1-D: custody walks the lexical path with per-prefix no-follow opens (no `EvalSymlinks`); root handle bound via `os.SameFile`.\\n- P1-E: create persists the binding doc; restore re-admits it through `termbind.ParseTerminalBinding` with agreement checks and returns it; after-restore branch (local lease → bounded 5000 ms refresh → resume/offer/park) wired and measured.\\n- P2-A: outcomes (with original timestamps) persisted per idempotency key and replayed; crash/retry paths attacked. Bound B34: receipt/outcome crash window re-observes time.\\n- P2-B: custody entry cells reclassified U2a → M with the reviewer's four exact shapes; symmetry paragraph carries per-side counts; ratio restated 208/4448 measured, 34 bound, 4206 unreachable; OUTCOME-keyed importer comparison over the 34-package closure: 2662 top-level + 20345 subtest shared inputs, zero moved, 205+169 additions all PASS in tmuxserver, zero removed.\\n- VALIDATION (exit 0, this run): gofmt/build/vet; full suite 45 ok (3083 top-level PASS in -v); race 45 ok no data races; cover (tmuxserver 87.4%); 17 fuzz gates; tracecheck; cataloggen -adopted -check; linux+windows builds; windows vet; JSON check; board validate (0 referencing this task); diff check; no-tmux proof (tmux hidden, 604 PASS); harness 210/210 (209 KILLED incl. 2 additive, 1 harmless control SURVIVED); 162/162 run masks match live tests.\\n- STATUS: ready for review; worktree intentionally UNCOMMITTED for Story handoff snapshot. Results standalone + matrix + `TASK-260830-1c28dz_rework-evidence-rev2.tar.gz` attached to the board item.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-1c28dz rework rev4 — rev3 CHANGES REQUESTED repaired on checkpoint d4bd91d\\n- SCOPE: second leaf of STORY-260830-2t4g7i, tmux lifecycle operations. All three P1 + P2-A + P2-B + the four surviving narrowings plus the SPW custody fifth closed in `internal/tmuxserver`; trunk unmoved, no rebase. Only touched landed files: error-code registry (new codes), ownership seam (test hook), mutant harnesses (new rows). Production `.go` delta is purely additive (0 deleted lines); all other production files are new.\\n- P1-A: quiesce/boundary barrier writes fail closed (`terminal_backend_integrity_failure` at `quiesce/boundary state image`); the outcome report commits first so retries replay the original closure time and heal the memory; attach recovers the barrier from completed closure outcomes when memory is missing (corrupt scan and empty time error). Five committed tests, seven narrowing rows.\\n- P1-B: the executed backend restore binds to the decided winner — carried `(lease_id, lease_epoch)` must equal the ordered winner or the entry refuses `local_precondition_failed` at `wrapper restore winner binding` before any effect. Three committed tests (joint + per-arm), two narrowing rows.\\n- P1-C: the refresh bound is enforced, not cooperative — the adapter runs on its own goroutine, the entry takes answer-or-deadline, late answers never verify (nil-error included), with a hook-stalled both-ready race test forcing the window deterministically. Two committed tests plus the reworked bound subtest (shared-var race removed, elapsed tightened 5s→1s), two narrowing rows. Bound B37 states the missing production mesh transport.\\n- R1-R5: exit-1 attached, foreign attached row, exit-2 panes, NUL argv, spawner root custody — five committed clause witnesses plus five harness rows with the reviewer's (corrected R5) plants; the SPW rootwrite cell moves B39→M.\\n- P2-B: Table C 19→18 U2c; totals recomputed by script (238 measured of 4896; 181 bound; 4477 unreachable); resume-reachable status cells U2a/U1→B39 (22 cells); row 83 stale names dropped and the successor order corrected (prior validation precedes effects; successor persists after); intro 92/92; wall-time prose corrected.\\n- P2-A: entry grid over pre-existing tmuxserver+termbind entries (27 keys, zero moves) plus new-entry behavior (27 keys, all ADDED); suite grid over the 34-package closure (23,054 shared keys, zero moves, 476 additions all PASS in tmuxserver+termbind, zero removed); drivers, streams, and diffs in the evidence tarball.\\n- VALIDATION (exit 0, this run): gofmt; build + vet unix and windows; full suite; race on both touched packages; cover (tmuxserver 87.7%, termbind 83.5%); tracecheck; cataloggen clean; harness 251/251 tmuxserver + 40/40 termbind with one raw log per plant.\\n- STATUS: ready for review; worktree intentionally UNCOMMITTED for Story handoff snapshot. Results standalone + matrix + `TASK-260830-1c28dz_rework-evidence-rev4.tar.gz` attached to the board item.\\n===git-diff-loogbook===\\ndiff --git a/LOGBOOK.md b/LOGBOOK.md\\nindex ff58edc..f2d3421 100644\\n--- a/LOGBOOK.md\\n+++ b/LOGBOOK.md\\n@@ -23,6 +23,15 @@\\n - VALIDATION: the fresh configured run is recorded under `.temp/BUG-260917-3lddu0/validation-rev3/`; all 30 configured commands exited 0. `task-board validate` reported 179 existing `MISSING_ACTIVITY` diagnostics and exited 0; scoped tracecheck §2.4 exited 0 and §5.3 exited 1 as the expected 7/8 refusal.\\n - HANDOFF: importer outcomes and tracecheck logs are task-scoped; the candidate remains UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree for snapshot handoff.\\n \\n+## 2026-09-22\\n+\\n+### TASK-260830-1c28dz — tmux lifecycle operations via structured commands (initial producer delivery)\\n+\\n+- SHIPPED the second `tmuxserver` leaf: `Execute` admits exactly the eight lifecycle operations (create, attach, status, quiesce, safe-boundary, stop, stale termination, restore) and refuses unknown ones; the exec adapter reconstructs the exact `tmux -S <socket> <subcommand>` vector per operation (forged binaries, flag injection, ambient discovery all refuse); the probed socket generation binds before execution (B18-B20); bodies are pure argv builders with the stable `ax pane SESSION_ID` entrypoint; effects run through the landed terminstance engine with strict per-operation deadlines, generation rechecks, and AX-side state memory, while attach/terminate/restore mirror the landed backend/fencing/axpane gates. Every mutating operation replays idempotently; uncertain receipts reconcile through status before resuming.\\n+- Battery: 173 narrowing + 2 additive KILLED + control SURVIVED (100 new second-leaf narrowing rows with per-arm killers; first leaf's 76 rows still green, shared control). AC: 33 of 33 rows (59-91) driven through production entries by named tests. Second-leaf census: Table B 24×21 (10 measured), Table C 90×11 (all unreachable), Table D 90×21 (108 measured), every measured cell with a named test plus an admitting narrowing row; singleton arms bound by B22, engine-normalized status by B23.\\n+- Full 30-command suite green firsthand on the frozen tree (gofmt, build, vet, full suite, race gate, cover, all fuzz gates, tracecheck, cataloggen, linux/windows builds, JSON check, board validate, diff check, windows vet); OUTCOME-keyed base-vs-candidate importer comparison clean (base 82 PASS retained, zero regressions). Evidence tarball with raw per-plant logs attached to `TASK-260830-1c28dz`. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\\n+- Process note: a full-suite cover gate failed while the mutant harness was still running in the same tree — the cover run compiled against a planted mutant. Re-ran clean after the harness exited 0. Never run `go test` concurrently with the harness in one worktree.\\n+\\n ## 2026-09-21\\n \\n ### BUG-260917-2fwf8e — fencing direction must beat lapsed-grant refusal\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 11186,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 2797,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
