{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000f86b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c836-a2d8-7092-9401-37d2858a2ec3"},"sequence":6800,"recorded_at":1780531400013595,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a68a1bdc-1b82-44d2-b715-51014e29fd57","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"a68a1bdc-1b82-44d2-b715-51014e29fd57","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a68a1bdc-1b82-44d2-b715-51014e29fd57"},"terminal":"completed","text":"Ready for review — handed off to review with checklist 25/25.\n\nWhat this round delivered, all on checkpoint `d4bd91d0` with the candidate left uncommitted:\n\n- **P1-A by construction**: the incarnation-scoped closure proof is now the sole barrier verdict. Closure reports bind the current incarnation; fresh create/restore successes rotate it (replays never rotate); failures install a first echo or the honest unknown but never overwrite; advisory memory is never consulted for admission. Both reviewer sequences run verbatim, plus reopen, replay-discipline, and rotation-failure sequences. New bounds B40 (stuck rotation, pinned mechanically against the landed one-bootstrap rule) and B41 (structural replay skip, D-row).\n- **P1-B composed authorization**: the wrapper join now covers session, bootstrap, admitted-descriptor instance/backend/generation, and winner lease/epoch, each with a divergence test and narrowing row; the 13-member identity census states what is joined vs deliberately unjoined with namespace/owner reasons. Both reviewer sequences verbatim. Table E grows to 22 outcomes.\n- **P2-B**: all four clause gaps witnessed with the reviewer plant shapes as harness rows; R3 closes the prober custody cell (B39→M).\n- **P2-A**: fixed-corpus production-entry outcome grid over the 36-package closure — 193 shared keys, zero moved, 7 declared candidate-only keys; suite verdicts 23,874 shared keys, zero moved. Found and fixed one grid flake (resumesmoke map-ordered member loop) and audited every member-naming error.\n- **P3**: B27 19→18, no-real-socket sentence corrected. Census recomputed by script: 250 measured of 5064; matrix mirrors verified byte-identical.\n\nValidation, all exit 0 firsthand: full suite both trees (45 ok each), race on both touched packages, cover (tmuxserver 88.0%), vet unix+windows, gofmt clean, harness 273/273 + 40/40 with one raw log per plant, no-tmux process audit clean, 6/6 grid determinism.\n\nEvidence attached: updated results and conformance matrix plus `TASK-260830-1c28dz_rework-evidence-rev5.tar.gz` (grid driver/streams/diffs, verdict streams, 313 per-plant logs, gate logs, SHA256SUMS).","reason":null}}
